  "title": "DataAccessV1dot17",
  "description": "K-05 v1.17, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1418: the architect's ruling on QUESTIONS.md CQ-342, option (d), on T-1417's NEED; DL-876, DL-877). It only adds to v1.16 (data-access.v1.16.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to every earlier version down to v1): every v1.16 definition is here under its own name, by reference, save the two restated: commitTurn.request, which takes the optional answerPhoneRowsBy, and commitTurn.exchange, to refer to it and to hold the answer of a request that asks to README item 71. So every v1 to v1.16 exchange is a v1.17 exchange. Added: with answerPhoneRowsBy handleId, every row reference commitTurn answers (committed.written, committed.waitingChat and versionChanged's changed) names a phones row by its handle id (K-04 v1 phones.handle_id), read from the row the commit locked or wrote, never by a second read, and every other table's row by its primary key, as rowRef says: an answered phones rowId is a K-08 v1 handleRef and never has phoneNumber's shape, and it is a name, never a key, so no request accepts it. Without the field the answer is v1.16's, byte for byte. New definitions: phoneRowByHandleId (one answered row reference, narrowed) and commitTurn.handleIdExchange (commitTurn.exchange narrowed by allOf to a request that asks, the definition the v1.17 fixtures are listed under). No call, state, column, grant, index or migration is added; rowRef, changedRow, promotion, commitTurn.response, commitTurn.errors and every request field of v1.16 are unchanged. Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
